exuberant, that things were more cynical today rather than exuberant. What do you mean by exuberant partisanship and how could we bring that back? One of the things I write about in the book is particularly in the conclusion is this is what appears to be a decline in this culture of democracy. And one element of that actually goes back a very long way. It's not just recent. So as you say, I think if you go back into the 19th century, partisanship was extremely, extremely strong. But there was a life in it, an excitement.
充满活力，现在的局势与其说是充满活力，不如说是愤世嫉俗。你所说的充满活力的党派性是什么意思，我们又该如何恢复它？我在书中写到的其中一件事，特别是在结论部分，就是这似乎是民主文化的一种衰落。而其中的一个要素实际上可以追溯到很久以前。它不仅仅是最近才出现的。正如你所说，我认为如果你追溯到19世纪，党派性非常非常强烈。但其中蕴含着生命力，一种兴奋感。

